{"tool_name":"pymzml","contents":["biocontainers","oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biocontainers":{"name":"pymzml","identifiers":["biotools:pymzml","doi:10.1093/bioinformatics/bts066","doi:10.1093/bioinformatics/bty046"],"license":"MIT","summary":"Python module to parse mzml data based on celementtree.","home_url":"https://github.com/pymzml/pymzML","keywords":["Data Compression","Mass Spectrometry","Proteomics","Proteomics experiment","Mass spectrometry"],"manually_check":true,"total_pulls":0},"biotools":{"id":"pymzml","home":"http://pymzml.github.com","license":"MIT","summary":"Python module to parse mzML data based on cElementTree.","addition_date":"2017-01-17T14:50:31Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T21:01:37.512560Z","tool_type":["Library"],"version":["2.4.1"],"collections":["Proteomics","ms-utils"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:pymzml","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"christian@fufezan.net","name":"Christian Fufezan","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Maintainer"]},{"email":"webmaster@ms-utils.org","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Documentor"],"url":"http://ms-utils.org"}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"https://pymzml.readthedocs.io/en/latest/"}],"edit_permission":{"authors":["JL-MS","StSchulze","fu","proteomics.bio.tools"],"type":"group"},"function":[{"input":[{"data":{"term":"Data","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_0006"},"format":[{"term":"mzML","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3244"}]}],"operation":[{"term":"Spectral analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3214"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"Data","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_0006"},"format":[{"term":"mzML","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3244"}]}]}],"maturity":"Mature","name":"pymzML","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"fu","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/bts066","metadata":{"abstract":"pymzML is an extension to Python that offers (i) an easy access to mass spectrometry (MS) data that allows the rapid development of tools, (ii) a very fast parser for mzML data, the standard data format in MS and (iii) a set of functions to compare or handle spectra. \u00a9 The Author 2012. Published by Oxford University Press. All rights reserved.","authors":[{"name":"Bald T."},{"name":"Barth J."},{"name":"Fufezan C."},{"name":"Hippler M."},{"name":"Niehues A."},{"name":"Specht M."}],"citationCount":70,"date":"2012-04-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Bioinformatics","title":"PymzML-Python module for high-throughput bioinformatics on mass spectrometry data"},"pmid":"22302572"},{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/bty046","metadata":{"abstract":"Motivation: In the new release of pymzML (v2.0), we have optimized the speed of this established tool for mass spectrometry data analysis to adapt to increasing amounts of data in mass spectrometry. Thus, we integrated faster libraries for numerical calculations, improved data retrieving algorithms and have optimized the source code. Importantly, to adapt to rapidly growing file sizes, we developed a generalizable compression scheme for very fast random access and applied this concept to mzML files to retrieve spectral data. Results: pymzML performs at par with established C programs when it comes to processing times. However, it offers the versatility of a scripting language, while adding unprecedented fast random access to compressed files. Additionally, we designed our compression scheme in such a general way that it can be applied to any field where fast random access to large data blocks in compressed files is desired. Availability and implementation: pymzML is freely available on https://github.com/pymzML/ pymzML under GPL license. pymzML requires Python3.4\u00fe and optionally numpy. Documentation available on http://pymzml.readthedocs.io.","authors":[{"name":"Fufezan C."},{"name":"Hippler M."},{"name":"Klein J."},{"name":"Kosters M."},{"name":"Leidel S.A."},{"name":"Leufken J."},{"name":"Schulze S."},{"name":"Sugimoto 